=   entry .Event   what running a command logs: starts, exits, aborts and kills
-     detail
+     detail

-         Every `Event` is tagged `Log.Process`. `ProcessStart(command)` is logged at `info` by
-         `fork`, `exec`, `detach` and a terminal session; `PipelineStart(commands)` likewise for
-         a pipeline; `ProcessExit(pid, code)` by `Job#exitStatus()`, at `fine` for zero and as
-         a warning otherwise; `AbortProcess(pid)` at `info` by `Job#abort()`; and
-         `KillProcess(pid)` as a warning by `Job#kill()`. An `Exec.Event is Loggable` must be
-         in scope wherever these run; `logging.silentLogging` discards them.
-     entry .communicable   renders each event as a message
+         Ogni `Event` ha il tag `Log.Process`. `ProcessStart(command)` viene registrato a livello
+         `info` da `fork`, `exec`, `detach` e da una sessione di terminale; `PipelineStart(commands)`
+         allo stesso modo per una pipeline; `ProcessExit(pid, code)` da `Job#exitStatus()`, a
+         livello `fine` per zero e come avviso altrimenti; `AbortProcess(pid)` a livello `info`
+         da `Job#abort()`; e `KillProcess(pid)` come avviso da `Job#kill()`. Un `Exec.Event is
+         Loggable` deve essere nell'ambito ovunque questi vengano eseguiti;
+         `logging.silentLogging` li scarta.
+     entry .communicable   rende ogni evento come un messaggio

